1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,200
You are nine years old, a prince in Kaifeng, and before you eat a single bite, a servant tastes it in case it kills you.

2
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:11,290
But poison is not what will break you.

3
00:00:11,790 --> 00:00:14,660
It is 969 AD

4
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:23,350
You live in Kaifeng, the capital of the Song Empire, on the plains of central China, just south of the Yellow River.

5
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:27,250
Today it is a city in China's Henan province.

6
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:30,790
The Song dynasty is only nine years old.

7
00:00:30,890 --> 00:00:33,250
The same age as you.

8
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:36,530
Every morning starts the same way.

9
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:41,710
The eunuch lifts your rice porridge to his own lips, swallows, and waits.

10
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:44,890
Everyone in the room watches his face.

11
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:47,780
If he turns pale, the cook dies.

12
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:50,100
If he smiles, you eat.

13
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,190
You eat slowly.

14
00:00:52,290 --> 00:00:55,990
Because the woman kneeling by the door taught you to.

15
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:58,270
"Small bites, my prince.

16
00:00:58,370 --> 00:01:00,580
If it tastes bitter, stop."

17
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:05,480
She is the same woman who tasted the milk nine years ago.

18
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:08,060
The palace calls her your nurse.

19
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:12,460
You call her something else, but only when no one is listening.

20
00:01:14,467 --> 00:01:17,827
At sunrise, you are taken to greet your mother.

21
00:01:17,927 --> 00:01:19,487
Your real mother.

22
00:01:19,587 --> 00:01:25,597
The consort who gave birth to you, and who has climbed the ranks of the palace because you lived.

23
00:01:26,097 --> 00:01:27,297
You kneel.

24
00:01:27,397 --> 00:01:30,197
You touch your forehead to the floor.

25
00:01:30,297 --> 00:01:34,147
She asks about your lessons, your health, your manners.

26
00:01:34,247 --> 00:01:36,157
She does not hug you.

27
00:01:36,257 --> 00:01:39,137
Princes are not hugged in public.

28
00:01:39,637 --> 00:01:42,077
To her, you are not just a son.

29
00:01:42,177 --> 00:01:43,957
You are her future.

30
00:01:44,057 --> 00:01:49,807
If you become Emperor one day, she becomes the most powerful woman in the empire.

31
00:01:49,907 --> 00:01:52,217
If you fail, she is nothing.

32
00:01:52,717 --> 00:01:55,417
Outside the hall, the nurse waits.

33
00:01:55,517 --> 00:01:57,847
She is not allowed inside.

34
00:01:57,947 --> 00:01:59,577
She is a servant.

35
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,550
Then come the lessons.

36
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:10,250
Your tutor is one of the most respected scholars in the empire, and he is not here to be kind.

37
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:14,210
You copy the classics, character by character.

38
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:17,220
You memorise the words of Confucius.

39
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:21,280
You learn history, morality, how a ruler should think.

40
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:24,350
One wrong stroke and you start again.

41
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:27,910
But your tutor is not only teaching you.

42
00:02:28,010 --> 00:02:29,640
He is watching you.

43
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:31,500
How clever you are.

44
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,050
How patient.

45
00:02:33,150 --> 00:02:35,590
How you react when you are wrong.

46
00:02:35,690 --> 00:02:38,840
Everything he sees can reach the Emperor.

47
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:41,930
So you never show you are tired.

48
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:44,640
You never show you are afraid.

49
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:47,800
You are nine, and you are already performing.

50
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:53,180
In the afternoon, a eunuch brings a message.

51
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:56,740
The Empress wishes to see you in her garden.

52
00:02:57,240 --> 00:03:00,450
She is the woman your nurse taught you to fear.

53
00:03:00,550 --> 00:03:05,020
The woman who, nine years ago, may have tried to poison your milk.

54
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:07,070
Today she smiles.

55
00:03:07,170 --> 00:03:09,970
She calls you a fine young prince.

56
00:03:10,070 --> 00:03:13,300
She offers you a sweet from a lacquered box.

57
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,900
Your hand reaches out.

58
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,650
Then you remember the voice at the door every morning.

59
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:21,830
You bow deeply.

60
00:03:21,930 --> 00:03:23,280
You thank her.

61
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:27,720
You say your tutor forbids sweets before evening lessons.

62
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:29,550
You do not take it.

63
00:03:30,050 --> 00:03:31,890
She smiles wider.

64
00:03:31,990 --> 00:03:36,650
And in that smile, you understand something no tutor ever taught you.

65
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:40,090
In the palace, kindness is a weapon too.

66
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:45,910
You have never walked through the city outside these walls.

67
00:03:46,010 --> 00:03:50,430
You have heard it: the drums, the markets, the carts, the shouting.

68
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:57,430
Some evenings you climb the garden stones to look at the rooftops of Kaifeng, glowing in the sunset.

69
00:03:57,930 --> 00:03:59,960
A hand pulls you down.

70
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:01,330
Your nurse.

71
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:05,210
"If a guard sees you, I will be beaten, not you."

72
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:11,270
You sit together against the wall, and you ask her the question you always ask.

73
00:04:11,370 --> 00:04:13,190
What is it like out there?

74
00:04:13,690 --> 00:04:19,160
She tells you about mud and rice fields and a little house by a willow tree.

75
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,780
Then she stops.

76
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,300
You know why.

77
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:26,590
Somewhere out there is the baby she left behind to feed you.

78
00:04:26,690 --> 00:04:29,360
Her child would be nine now too.

79
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:31,650
She has never seen them again.

80
00:04:33,667 --> 00:04:36,107
At night, she is the one who stays.

81
00:04:36,207 --> 00:04:37,967
She checks the windows.

82
00:04:38,067 --> 00:04:40,167
She tastes your water.

83
00:04:40,267 --> 00:04:43,727
She sits by your bed until your eyes close.

84
00:04:44,227 --> 00:04:49,737
And tonight, half asleep, you whisper the word you are never allowed to say out loud.

85
00:04:50,237 --> 00:04:51,867
"Goodnight, mother."

86
00:04:52,367 --> 00:04:53,827
She freezes.

87
00:04:53,927 --> 00:04:58,817
Then she presses her hand over your mouth, gently, and looks at the door.

88
00:04:58,917 --> 00:05:05,217
Because if the consort ever hears you call a servant "mother", the nurse will be sent away.

89
00:05:05,317 --> 00:05:06,587
Or worse.

90
00:05:07,087 --> 00:05:09,487
She kisses your forehead.

91
00:05:09,587 --> 00:05:11,237
She says nothing.

92
00:05:11,337 --> 00:05:15,207
But she does not stop crying until the candle goes out.

93
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:19,583
This prince is our story.

94
00:05:19,683 --> 00:05:24,903
But what happened to him really did happen to a prince of the Song dynasty.

95
00:05:25,403 --> 00:05:30,933
In 1010, a palace maid named Lady Li gave birth to the Emperor's son.

96
00:05:31,033 --> 00:05:37,723
But the baby was claimed by her mistress, the powerful Consort Liu, who raised him as her own.

97
00:05:37,823 --> 00:05:41,263
The boy grew up believing Liu was his mother.

98
00:05:41,763 --> 00:05:47,273
At 12 he became Emperor Renzong, and Liu ruled for him as regent.

99
00:05:47,373 --> 00:05:52,013
His real mother lived in the same palace, and she kept her silence.

100
00:05:52,513 --> 00:05:57,173
Only after Liu died in 1033 did he learn the truth.

101
00:05:57,273 --> 00:06:00,943
His birth mother had already died the year before.

102
00:06:01,043 --> 00:06:07,053
He wept at her coffin and gave her the title she never had in life: Empress Dowager.

103
00:06:07,553 --> 00:06:12,723
He went on to rule for 41 years, the longest of any Song emperor.

104
00:06:12,823 --> 00:06:18,993
And for most of his life, the woman who gave birth to him was a stranger in his own palace.

105
00:06:19,493 --> 00:06:23,473
The history books remember emperors and empresses.

106
00:06:23,573 --> 00:06:29,423
They rarely remember the maids, the nurses and the mothers who raised them in the shadows.

107
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:34,073
So tonight, ask yourself: who really raised the emperor?
